# The tutorial's words, ported from data/tutorial.json (prompt 03) without changing them.
# data/tutorial.json keeps the structure (lessons, goals, what to point at, the queries);
# magic/tutorial.py puts these lines back in their places when it loads the tutorial.
# Nodes: <lesson>_<part> (intro, demo_after, task, restate, off_goal, success), opening,
# ending, practice_<quest>_done, practice_<quest>_label, coach_<name>, dummy_<pool>.
# In a step, a Grimoire line (or a narrator line, ': text') starts the step; a Training Dummy
# line after it is the dummy's reply in the same step. {rows}, {cast}, {lost}, {page},
# {mp_before}, {mp_after} are filled in from the real result. See docs/WRITING.md.

== opening ==
Grimoire: Before any guardian: practice. This straw dummy cannot hurt you. Nothing here can.
Training Dummy: I can judge you, though.

== look_intro ==
Grimoire: A query asks a table for its rows. Watch me ask the table called enemies.

== look_demo_after ==
Grimoire: One row, one creature: the dummy. Each column is one fact about it.
Training Dummy: Take a picture. It lasts longer.

== look_task ==
Grimoire: Your turn. Write the same query:

== look_restate ==
Grimoire: Ask the table enemies for everything:

== look_off_goal ==
Grimoire: A real query! But I asked for the dummy:

== look_success ==
Grimoire: There it is again, and this time you asked. Your first query!

== columns_intro ==
Grimoire: My page is narrow: a wide row gets cut at the right edge. So ask for less.

== columns_demo_after ==
Grimoire: Two names after SELECT, a comma between them: two columns on the page.

== columns_task ==
Grimoire: Your turn. Find what the dummy is weak to:

== columns_restate ==
Grimoire: Two columns from enemies, name and weakness:

== columns_off_goal ==
Grimoire: Good look! But its weakness is not there:

== columns_success ==
Grimoire: Fire. Remember it: a foe's weakness takes double damage.
Training Dummy: Rude. That was private.

== read_intro ==
Grimoire: All those looks, and your MP has not moved. Looking is free. Read before you act.

== read_demo_after ==
Grimoire: Your spells. None of them fired: I left out the name column on purpose.

== read_task ==
Grimoire: Your turn. Read three columns of your spells:

== read_restate ==
Grimoire: Three columns from the table spells:

== read_off_goal ==
Grimoire: Nice, but I want to see each spell's element:

== read_success ==
Grimoire: The first spell is Fire, and the dummy is weak to Fire. Only 3 MP, too.
Training Dummy: I do not like where this is going.

== cast_intro ==
Grimoire: Now the magic. A row that carries a spell's name casts that spell. Watch.

== cast_demo_after ==
Grimoire: {cast} spells fired, and Fire hit twice as hard. But read the rest.
Training Dummy: Ow. Ow. Ow. Ow. In that order.
Grimoire: My page holds {page} rows. The other {lost} fell off the bottom and fizzled.
Grimoire: Yet I paid for all {rows}: MP {mp_before} to {mp_after}. That is the Rule of the Page.
Grimoire: Here, I refill your mana. Guardians will not be so kind.

== cast_task ==
Grimoire: Your turn. Attack the dummy: ask the table spells for its name column.

== cast_restate ==
Grimoire: Spell names are triggers. Ask for them:

== cast_off_goal ==
Grimoire: Nothing hit the dummy. Ask spells for name:

== cast_success ==
Grimoire: Real magic! And you overflowed the page, like every witch on day one.
Training Dummy: My straw! My only straw!
Grimoire: {cast} hit, {lost} fizzled, {rows} paid for. I refill your mana once more.

== practice_intro ==
Grimoire: Free practice. Nothing can go wrong here. TABLES (F4) lists what you can ask.

== practice_task ==
Grimoire: Try these if you like. Press F5 when you feel READY.

== practice_element_label ==
: Put your own element on the page

== practice_element_done ==
Grimoire: Arcane. Neither strong nor weak against anything. Like a spreadsheet.

== practice_book_label ==
: Read the dummy's spell book

== practice_book_done ==
Grimoire: Empty: it knows no spells. A guardian's book will not be. Read it.
Training Dummy: Straw does not retain much.

== practice_log_label ==
: Read the world's diary: query_log

== practice_log_done ==
Grimoire: Every query ever cast here, yours included. This world forgets nothing.
Training Dummy: I remember EVERYTHING.

== practice_all_done ==
Grimoire: All three! You read tables better than most witches. F5 when READY.

== ending ==
Grimoire: One thing should bother you: you wanted ONE spell, and you paid for all of them.
Grimoire: There is a rune for that. The next guardian knows it. Watch its book.
Grimoire: All I showed you is in the GUIDE (F3). Open it whenever you are lost.
: Something round and green wobbles out of the bushes: the ASTERISK SLIME!
Training Dummy: Not my problem. Good luck!

== coach_miscast ==
Grimoire: No harm done: a miscast is free. Try this:

== coach_undone ==
Grimoire: Nothing breaks in practice: I put it back.

== coach_enter ==
Grimoire: ENTER makes a new line. CTRL+ENTER casts.

== coach_cast_hint ==
Grimoire: CTRL+ENTER casts it

== coach_cast_too_early ==
Grimoire: Oops: those names fired spells! That is next.

== coach_ghost_word ==
Grimoire: Follow the faded word: TAB takes it.

== coach_offer ==
Grimoire: Stuck? Press TAB and I will write it with you.

== coach_refill ==
Grimoire: I refill your mana. In here it is free.

== coach_practice_miscast ==
Grimoire: No harm done. Read the red note and try again.

== coach_looks_spent ==
Grimoire: A turn has 3 free looks. In here, have more.

== coach_skip ==
Grimoire: Skip the tutorial?  ENTER: skip   ESC: stay

== coach_continue ==
Grimoire: ENTER

== dummy_looked_at ==
Training Dummy: Stop staring. I am shy.
Training Dummy: Yes, that is all of me.
Training Dummy: My good side is the left.
Training Dummy: Read me like a book. Ha.

== dummy_hit ==
Training Dummy: Ow. I am a prop, you know.
Training Dummy: My straw! My only straw!
Training Dummy: I felt that in my seams.
Training Dummy: Was that really necessary?

== dummy_miscast ==
Training Dummy: Even I could spell that.
Training Dummy: I felt nothing. Literally.
Training Dummy: The grammar hurt, though.

== dummy_restuffed ==
Training Dummy: *stuffs its straw back in*

== dummy_idle ==
Training Dummy: Take your time. I am straw.
Training Dummy: I am not going anywhere.
